title: Introducing Custom Markers for Advanced Users
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Custom-markup lets you raise the level of abstraction. Instead of repeating a long class chain like `».indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-primary` on every paragraph, give that combination a name and use the name everywhere.

In v1.0 there are two ways to give a class chain a name: a ''marker tiddler'' (canonical, wiki-wide) or an inline ''pragma'' (escape hatch, scoped to one tiddler).

!! Without abstraction

This works but is long, error-prone, and obscures the prose:

```
».indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-primary Some primary box text.
».indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-success Some success box text.
».indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-warning Some warning box text.
```

See [[Basics for advanced users]] for the underlying class chain.

!! Option 1: marker tiddlers (canonical, vocabulary-engine)

Define one marker tiddler per named style, tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker>>:

|! Field |! `PRIMARY` marker |! `SUCCESS` marker |! `WARNING` marker |
|`open` |`PRIMARY` |`SUCCESS` |`WARNING` |
|`kind` |`word` |`word` |`word` |
|`mode` |`block` |`block` |`block` |
|`element` |`p` |`p` |`p` |
|`classes` |`.indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-primary` |`.indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-success` |`.indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-warning` |

Group them under a vocabulary tag (e.g. `vocab/color-boxes`) and add a meta tiddler titled `vocab/color-boxes` tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary>>.

Activate where needed:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Color-Boxes
```

Then write the prose plainly:

```
PRIMARY Some primary box text.

SUCCESS Some success box text.

WARNING Some warning box text.
```

The blank line between each block is the default block terminator.

!! Option 2: inline pragma (escape hatch)

If you only need the abstraction in a single tiddler, the legacy `\custom` pragma binds a name to a class chain right at the top of the text:

```
\custom angle=primary _classes=".indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-primary"
\custom angle=success _classes=".indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-success"
\custom angle=warning _classes=".indent.right-dedent.justify.cbox.cbox-warning"

»primary Some primary box text.
»success Some success box text.
»warning Some warning box text.
```

The pragma form only affects the current tiddler. The marker-tiddler form makes the abstraction available wiki-wide, opt-in per type field.

A worked example lives at [[Example - Color-box word markers]].

See [[Custom Markup Definition]] for the full pragma parameter list and [[Vocabulary Engine]] for the marker-field schema. Pre-built reusable pragmas live in [[Import Predefined Pragmas]].
